    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24779" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-viscĕro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to put into the entrails</i>
			(post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid canibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nemes. Cyn. 214</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caritas inviscerata in cordibus nostris,</span>”
				<i>deeply rooted</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Serm. 24</span></i>
			.</div>
